in this we learned how to deploy a java app using jenkins, maven and tomcat
maven is a tool used to build and testing the code 
tomcat is a tool user for deploying the code
basically used in/for application server
what we done is we forked the code from a repo and build it on jenkins its a java code
befor building the code we need to add the maven tool in jenkins 

jenkins> manage jenkins (settings) > tools> maven installations> 
configure> build steps> add maven> name it> goals> type "clean package" > save it

now make ur first build in the home> u will see a folder names target ( where source code is present)
now we need a application ser for using tomcat to avoid the heavy load on the pipeline 
launch new server with t3.micro is enough for this application & open the server using another putty/ console
install tomcat in this new server,
for that open "dicdn.appache.org" website and open tomcat folder and open tomcat version 9
(we are using this version for running this application) and check the present version which is 9.0.112

here is the script for this :

yum install java-17-amazon-corretto -y
wget https://dlcdn.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.112/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.112.tar.gz
tar -zxvf apache-tomcat-9.0.112.tar.gz
sed -i '56  a\<role rolename="manager-gui"/>' apache-tomcat-9.0.112/conf/tomcat-users.xml
sed -i '57  a\<role rolename="manager-script"/>' apache-tomcat-9.0.112/conf/tomcat-users.xml
sed -i '58  a\<user username="tomcat" password="admin@123" roles="manager-gui, manager-script"/>' apache-tomcat-9.0.112/conf/tomcat-users.xml
sed -i '59  a\</tomcat-users>' apache-tomcat-9.0.112/conf/tomcat-users.xml
sed -i '56d' apache-tomcat-9.0.112/conf/tomcat-users.xml
sed -i '21d' apache-tomcat-9.0.112/webapps/manager/META-INF/context.xml
sed -i '22d'  apache-tomcat-9.0.112/webapps/manager/META-INF/context.xml
sh apache-tomcat-9.0.112/bin/startup.sh

now in new local server create a new file and use this command
vim appserver.sh> insert mode> paste the above commands> save and quit> sh appserver.sh
# here sh means shell script, we used sh to execute all the commands at a time.

now paste the ip address of tomcat server in new tab followed by port number
for example 3.226.76.130:8080> directs to tomcat dashboard> manager app> login using the crediantials mentions in the installation script
username: tomcat > password: admin@123
after login this is where our application runs
to see our app here buid in jenkins after installing the tomcat plugin
jenkins> manage jenkins> plugins> available plugins> search deploy to container> install
home> our job> configure> post build action > deploy war/ear to container> give the war,ear file name "target*/.war" (when we need all the war files to be added)
next context path > random server name( e-commerce)
now containers> select tomcat 9.x remote> add crediantials> username> password> id- appserver> description> save
add tomcat url> save
build> check in tomcat dashboard e-commerce app will be visible> click on it boom app is deployed

